{
  "name": "How to Plan Your Bathroom Vanity Upgrade",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Ready to give your bathroom a fresh look with a new vanity? Let’s walk through the typical steps. First, it’s all about measuring. You need to accurately measure the space where your vanity will go, including its width, depth, and height. Don’t forget to consider clearances for doors and drawers! Next, you’ll want to shut off the water supply to your old vanity and disconnect the plumbing. This is where things get a bit wet, so be prepared with towels! Then, it's time to carefully remove your old vanity. Sometimes this is easy, sometimes it requires a bit of persuasion. After the old one is out, you'll place and secure your new vanity cabinet. This often involves leveling it and attaching it to the wall. The exciting part comes next: connecting the sink and faucet plumbing. Make sure all your connections are tight and secure to avoid leaks. Finally, you’ll seal the edges around the sink and where the vanity meets the wall to protect against water. After all that, test everything for leaks before you declare the project done. For trickier setups or if you're moving plumbing, HH Remodeling LLC can help make sure it’s done right.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
